  q(MICRO,'A college student has fever, a stiff neck and a purple rash. Which organism is most likely?','Neisseria meningitidis',['Neisseria gonorrhoeae','Escherichia coli','Candida albicans'],'B','Meningococcal disease spreads in close living quarters and is prevented with vaccines.',EST),
  q(PARA,'Which tapeworm is spread by raw fish and can cause vitamin B12 deficiency?','Diphyllobothrium latum',['Taenia solium','Echinococcus granulosus','Enterobius vermicularis'],'C','The fish tapeworm absorbs vitamin B12 in the intestine, leading to anemia.',EST),
  q(PARA,'Which tick-borne parasite infects red blood cells and may form a “Maltese cross” pattern?','Babesia',['Giardia','Plasmodium vivax','Toxoplasma'],'D','Babesiosis is spread by the same deer tick that spreads Lyme disease.',EST),
  q(PARA,'Which mosquito-borne worm blocks lymph vessels and can cause elephantiasis?','Wuchereria bancrofti',['Ascaris lumbricoides','Trichinella spiralis','Schistosoma mansoni'],'A','The microfilariae are often found in blood drawn at night, when they circulate in the peripheral blood.',EST),
  q(PARA,'Which amoeba enters through the nose in warm fresh water and attacks the brain?','Naegleria fowleri',['Entamoeba histolytica, which affects the gut and liver','Giardia lamblia','Trichomonas vaginalis'],'B','This rare infection is almost always fatal, so nose clips are advised in warm lakes.',EST)
